# Intent: Time-of-day face variants (features.md, Faces and look; off by default). maipai_face_tod_core.h is plain C: four bands (morning, day, evening, night) that start at the hours in the face settings, night running through midnight; a unit whose clock was never set, or with the setting off, stays in the day look. A band changes only two things: how far the eyelids may open (full, full, 90 percent, 70 percent; DefaultEyes::setLidCap, kept on top of blink and emotion) and how bright the drawing colour is (100, 100, 85, 55 percent). maipai_face.cc starts one LVGL timer at one second, the shared face tick, that redraws only when the band changes; turning the setting on or off through self.face.set_config redraws at once. Behind CONFIG_MAIPAI_FACE_TOD (default y); off, no band code is compiled.
# Placement: unit (the face and the clock run on the robot)
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/eyes.cpp of the StackChan tree (MIT); new file hal/maipai_face_tod_core.h
# Check after a flash: self.face.set_config {"tod":true,"tod_hours":[6,9,18,21]}: at 22:00 the lids sit lower and the face is softer; at noon it is the plain face; {"tod":false} returns the plain face at once.
